            <ArticleTitle>[Central hemodynamics, kidney functions and water-salt metabolism in patients with ischemic heart disease and an increased venous blood return to the heart].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study is presented of the central hemodynamics, renal function and water-salt metabolism in 42 patients with ischemic heart disease and chronic circulatory insufficiency (grades I and II) and revealed a deterioration of these indices in this categories of patients manifested in a retention of sodium, deterioration of central hemodynamics after increase of venous inflow.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
